  --installation <id>
    The WHMCS installation that made
    the request (its BladeCP
    installation ID, a UUID)
  --client <id>
    The client of that installation the
    request belongs to (its client ID
    in WHMCS)
  -w, --watch
    Keep following the request until it
    needs someone or ends

  A request is named by the WHMCS
  installation and the client that made
  it: --installation is the BladeCP
  installation ID of that WHMCS, and
  --client the client ID in it. The
  BladeCP WHMCS module sends the same
  values.

  Examples ────────────────────────────
  › bladecp partner migrations show
    01979f2c-0000-7000-8000-000000000002
    --installation
    01980000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a1
    --client 42
    Phase, preview and billing of a
    request
  › bladecp partner migrations show
    01979f2c --installation
    01980000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a1
    --client 42 --watch
